{"id": "gv-016", "variant": "rs397508070", "gene": "KCNQ1", "difficulty": "hard", "classification": "Classification: Uncertain Significance\nCriteria used: PS3, PP3 \n\nNote: While the variant is a splice donor variant with high impact and predicted to be pathogenic by multiple lines of computational evidence (PP3), it is also present at an extremely low frequency in the general population (PM2). These conflicting criteria do not meet the thresholds for a confident call. BA1 does not apply here as the allele frequency is below 5%.", "evidence_text": "-- ClinVar (one submitter assertion, not the final answer) --\nHGVS: NM_000218.3(KCNQ1):c.1032+1G>T\nClinVar significance: Pathogenic\nReview status: criteria provided, single submitter\n\nHGVS: NM_000218.3(KCNQ1):c.1032+1G>C\nClinVar significance: Pathogenic\nReview status: criteria provided, single submitter\n\nHGVS: NM_000218.3(KCNQ1):c.1032+1G>A\nClinVar significance: Pathogenic/Likely pathogenic\nReview status: criteria provided, multiple submitters, no conflicts\n\n-- Population frequency (gnomAD) --\nAllele frequency: 6.569956901082729e-06\n\n-- Predicted consequence (Ensembl VEP) --\nMost severe consequence: splice_donor_variant (impact=HIGH)\nGene: KCNQ1\n\n-- Conservation (UCSC) --\nphyloP=9.23495, phastCons=1\n\n-- Computational pathogenicity (AlphaMissense) --\nNot applicable (non-missense variant).", "criteria_text": "[acmg_criteria.md]\n# ACMG/AMP Variant Classification Criteria > Condensed development sample summarizing the ACMG/AMP 2015 framework (Richards et al.). > For the authoritative text, see the full guideline (acmg.net / PMC) and ClinGen gene-specific > specifications. This file exists to exercise the retrieval pipeline, not as a clinical reference. A variant is classified by collecting evidence criteria, each with a direction (pathogenic or benign) and a strength (stand-alone, very strong, strong, moderate, or supporting), then combining them into a 5-tier call. ## Pathogenic criteria - **PVS1 (